This is **Erdős Problem 1167** from erdosproblems.com, a problem of Erdős, Hajnal, and Rado. It asks whether the **stepping-down** converse of the classical Erdős–Rado stepping-up lemma holds:

- **Stepping-up (known theorem, Erdős–Rado):** For $r \geq 2$, $\gamma \geq 2$:
$$\lambda \to (\kappa_\alpha)_{\alpha<\gamma}^r \implies 2^\lambda \to (\kappa_\alpha + 1)_{\alpha<\gamma}^{r+1}$$

- **Stepping-down (this problem, open):** Does the converse hold?
$$2^\lambda \to (\kappa_\alpha + 1)_{\alpha<\gamma}^{r+1} \implies \lambda \to (\kappa_\alpha)_{\alpha<\gamma}^r$$

