The partition relation $\mu \to (\nu_\alpha)_{\alpha<\gamma}^r$ means: every $r$-coloring (here, $\gamma$-coloring) of the $r$-element subsets of $\mu$ admits a monochromatic subset of size $\nu_\alpha$ in color $\alpha$ for some $\alpha$. The stepping-up lemma uses a coding argument (encoding pairs from $2^\lambda$ via elements of $\lambda$) to lift partition relations from exponent $r$ to $r+1$. The **converse** would require extracting an $r$-uniform coloring on $\lambda$ from an $(r+1)$-uniform coloring on $2^\lambda$, which is a fundamentally different and much harder task — no known technique accomplishes this in general.

